## **Viewing Instance and Process Information**

In Oracle, you can query dynamic performance views (V$ views) to see instance and process information:

sql

```
-- See instance information
SELECT INSTANCE_NAME, STATUS, DATABASE_STATUS 
FROM V$INSTANCE;

-- See all background processes
SELECT PNAME, DESCRIPTION 
FROM V$BGPROCESS 
WHERE PADDR != '00';

-- See SGA component sizes
SELECT COMPONENT, CURRENT_SIZE/1024/1024 AS SIZE_MB 
FROM V$SGA_DYNAMIC_COMPONENTS;

-- See overall SGA summary
SELECT NAME, VALUE/1024/1024 AS SIZE_MB 
FROM V$SGA;

```

---

## **Summary**

**Instance = SGA + Background Processes**

{% table %}
- **Background Process**
- **Key Responsibility**
---
- DBWn
- Writes dirty buffers to data files
---
- LGWR
- Writes redo log buffer to redo log files
---
- CKPT
- Records checkpoint info in control file
---
- SMON
- Instance recovery, free space management
---
- PMON
- Cleans up failed user processes and their locks
---
- ARCn
- Archives filled redo log files
---
- MMON
- AWR snapshots, ADDM, alerts
---
- RECO
- Resolves failed distributed transactions
---
- LREG
- Registers instance with the listener
{% /table %}
